-- §9  Across every kind of search this model defines, how often did somebody actually look?
# One row per (kind of search, answer). Two questions are asked of documents about their own
# diligence, did you look for couplings between your layers and did you look for double counting
# across your parts, and this is the only place both are counted together.
#
# Neither half gives this number
#   epistemics/coupling_searches.sqlc and eliminations/searched.sqlc each answer for one
#   question; the union answers for the model. "How often does anybody look at all" is a fact
#   about the practice rather than about either mechanism, and it needs both arms in one relation
#   to be askable.
#
# A NULL answer is not an absence
#   It means the document filed the thing itself, real couplings or real eliminations, so the
#   search question is answered by the content. Counting it as a refusal would report a document
#   that did the work as one that declined it.
-- epistemics/searches.sqlc, folded by question and answer.
SELECT s.looked_for                                   AS "looked_for!",
       coalesce(s.answer::text, 'filed the thing')    AS "answer!",
       count(*)                                       AS "times!"
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/searches.sqlc)
) s
GROUP BY s.looked_for, s.answer
ORDER BY s.looked_for, count(*) DESC, 2
